  "stem": "A block A of mass 4 kg is placed on another block B of mass 5 kg, and the block B rests on smooth horizontal table. If the minimum force that can be applied on block A so that it slips over B is 12 N, then the maximum force that can be applied on block B for the blocks to move together will be?",
  "options": {
    "A": "48 N",
    "B": "27 N",
    "C": "15 N",
    "D": "40/3 N"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "C"
    ]
  },
